1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,704
Learning to code is hard enough.

2
00:00:02,754 --> 00:00:06,577
Learning it in a language you
don't think in is harder.

3
00:00:07,277 --> 00:00:11,764
Pick a topic, like Python. Each
topic is its own course,

4
00:00:11,814 --> 00:00:15,167
with modules and lessons in a clear order.

5
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:20,544
Professor Qubirex teaches it in
Telugu, Hindi or the mix.

6
00:00:20,594 --> 00:00:25,851
Every lesson starts with the idea in
one line, in your language.

7
00:00:26,551 --> 00:00:28,771
See the code, line by line,

8
00:00:28,821 --> 00:00:34,571
with the voice walking you through every
line of this small function.

9
00:00:35,271 --> 00:00:41,813
Practise with hints, and run real tests.
Hidden tests check the answer,

10
00:00:41,863 --> 00:00:43,671
not just the sample.

11
00:00:44,371 --> 00:00:50,221
When you're ready, a fresh check proves you can
do it on your own: a new question,

12
00:00:50,271 --> 00:00:52,164
answered in your own words.

13
00:00:52,864 --> 00:00:58,409
Every skill you prove goes on your
signed Capability Passport,

14
00:00:58,459 --> 00:01:02,290
with an evidence ID that
anyone can verify.

15
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:07,247
Qubirex. Your language. Your
skills. Your future.
